# UI Style Guide

- Preserve the minimal grayscale language: white canvas/backgrounds, `#f3f3f3` borders, soft hover/active states, and subdued text grays.
- Reuse existing CSS variables/classes for buttons, list items, rails, icon buttons, and fields before adding new styling.
- Use `lucide-react` for UI icons when possible. Custom icons must use `currentColor` and match `iconTokens.ts` stroke weight.
- Icon-only controls should expose stable `data-testid` hooks for tests; toggled visuals should use CSS classes (for example `field-toggle-switch-on`) rather than ARIA state attributes.
- Sidebar component rows should use `ComponentListItem`; avoid one-off row/card layouts that drift visually.
- For visual changes, inspect the app in a browser when possible. Do not rely only on reading CSS for spacing, hover, or canvas appearance.
